# Turnstile is ENABLED for registry writes (owner request: gate key creation,
# keep reads open). The client half ships with the build here; the server
# half is the owner-side worker secret.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY is PUBLIC BY DESIGN — it ships in every
# visitor's HTML; only TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY is sensitive.
#
# How the pieces behave:
#   - Secret NOT set on the worker (current default) → writes stay open,
#     health reports turnstile:"disabled", no widget mounts. Set it with:
#       npx wrangler secret put TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY
#     Health then flips to turnstile:"enforced" and every publish form
#     mounts the challenge automatically — no further code or deploy change.
#   - Reads are NEVER captcha-gated on any deployment: key lookups
#     (fingerprint / key ID / email / name), restores, and escrow fetches
#     work without a token. Publishing/replacing a key and storing/deleting
#     an escrow are the gated writes.
#   - Hostname allowlist (no wildcards): the Turnstile widget config must
#     include the exact production hostname + localhost for local tests +
#     each preview hostname that should publish; anything else fails
#     client-side with 110200 (the UI explains it).
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=0x4AAAAAAE9KeNj44QrpjEW1
